From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/90] Block facts from a binary snapshot instead of 3.3 GB of
 JSON each start

Decoding gameplay-facts.json (3.3 GB with 184 mods) and block-behaviours.json took 13 s of the core load each start. The decoded facts and gameplay projection are kept in .horizon-cache/block-facts-v1.bin (postcard + lz4, 23 MB), keyed by the source files' sizes and times, the registry size and the decoder's own sources; anything unreadable or stale falls back to the JSON, which stays authoritative. HORIZON_FACTS_SNAPSHOT_CHECK=1 decodes both and compares every field.

UMP, 184 mods warm: core 17-19.5 s -> 10-11 s; the check says the snapshot equals the JSON. Ready time unchanged (89-98 s): the Java mods' start is the critical path. Unit test: capture/restore round trip.
